<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Augusto Pinochet</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1915–2006</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Augusto Pinochet was a Chilean general who led the military coup of 11 September 1973 that overthrew <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/salvador-allende">Salvador Allende</a>. He ruled Chile as dictator until 1990, with widespread repression and free-market economic reforms, and imposed the constitution of 1980. After losing the plebiscite of 1988 he handed power to an elected president.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/augusto-pinochet.jpg" alt="Augusto Pinochet" width="320" height="431" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ministerio de Relaciones Exteriores de Chile · CC BY 2.0 cl · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Augusto_Pinochet_foto_oficial(b).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
